WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.490
Rwanda grows coffee and tea,
and sells metal ores abroad.

2
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:11.830
From April to June 2025, Rwanda's domestic
exports earned 346 million dollars.

3
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:17.130
In the same months of 2026,
they earned 549 million.

4
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.470
That is a jump of 59 per
cent in a single year.

5
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.090
More money from abroad
sounds like good news.

6
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.570
So why could a jump like
that be bad news too?

7
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:30.430
Isn't more exports simply more money?

8
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.530
In this mission, you'll map
who buys Rwanda's exports,

9
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.770
and what foreign companies
bring to the country.

10
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.090
Then you'll weigh the
gains and costs of aid,

11
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.050
and of debt relief.

12
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:46.210
Your mission: explain why an export
boom can be bad news as well as good.
